# core/data/talk/grammar/en/beats_more.tlk - T5b-TOPIC: more lines for the drama manager's own
# rules, so a long session stops repeating the starter bank of beats_lines.tlk (T6-DM saw it
# repeat). Same guards, same acts, new rule names (<name>.more): the generator reads every rule
# whose name starts with the fixed name. Kid-safe except the adult-only beats, which keep the
# guards of their starter rules. Syntax: core/tools/talkc_gen.py; docs/TALK.md "The drama manager".

# ---- ARRIVE ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.arrive.more guard: beat=arrive act: tell
  "There you are! I saved you the lumpy chair."
  "Come in, {you}. Mind the draft. It's friendly."
  "Oh good, company. I was about to talk to the toaster."
  "Hello, {you}! Wipe your feet. Or don't, the rug is used to it."
  "You're here! Quick, look casual. I'll look casual too."
  "Welcome, {you}. We've been expecting someone. You'll do nicely."

# ---- SMALLTALK ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.smalltalk.more guard: beat=smalltalk act: tell
  "I had a thought this morning. It left before lunch."
  "My knees say rain. My knees also say a lot of things."
  "The kettle and I had words. It won."
  "Did you notice the light? Funny shade today."
  "I tried a new route to the shop. It was the same route."
  "Somebody parked a goat outside. Nobody knows whose."
  "I slept well. Suspiciously well. I checked for gaps."
@rule beat.smalltalk.ask.more guard: beat=smalltalk act: ask_about
  "What's the best thing you ate this week, {you}? Be honest."
  "How are the shoes, {you}? Comfortable? Haunted?"
  "Tell me one good thing, {you}. A small one counts."

# ---- TOPIC_DIVE -------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.topic_dive.more guard: beat=topic_dive&topic act: opine_pos
  "Hold on, {x}? I wrote a song about {x.it}. It's short."
  "{x:cap}! Say more. Say it slowly, I'm taking notes."
  "If we're doing {x}, I'm getting snacks first."
  "I've waited years for someone to bring up {x}. Years."
  "Talking about {x}? I'm in. I'm fully in."
  "{x:cap} is my specialist subject. I'll bring the chart."

# ---- HOUSE ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.house.more guard: beat=house act: tell
  "The floorboards are playing a tune. Listen. Off-key."
  "Is it me, or is this house leaning toward the kitchen?"
  "I like it here. The walls have a lived-in look."
  "That corner is empty. Needs a plant. Or a plan."
  "The clock has been four-twenty for a week. I respect it."
  "Cosy, {you}. In a slightly spooky way. The best way."

# ---- GOSSIP ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.gossip.more guard: beat=gossip act: gossip
  "Psst. Somebody put a hat on the statue. Nobody knows who."
  "Rumour has it the bakery's changing its recipe. I'm sorry."
  "They say the mayor snores in meetings. I say that's a gift."
  "I heard something. Then I heard it differently. Choose one."
  "Don't repeat this. I'm repeating it, but you don't."
  "There's a new face in town. Taller than the last one."

# ---- PROBLEM ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.problem.more guard: beat=problem&fact.problem act: complain
  "Do you have a minute? It's about something small. It's not small."
  "I don't want to be a bother. But it's been on my chest all week."
  "I keep saying I'm fine. It's getting a little tired of me."
  "Something's off, {you}. I can't put a finger on it."
@rule beat.problem.lonely.more guard: beat=problem&prob=lonely act: complain
  "The house is so quiet it hums. I talk to the plants."
  "I set two cups out this morning. Out of habit."
@rule beat.problem.bored.more guard: beat=problem&prob=bored act: complain
  "I counted the ceiling tiles. Twice. They disagreed."
  "I'm so bored I read the back of the cereal box. Out loud."
@rule beat.problem.nightmare.more guard: beat=problem&prob=nightmare act: complain
  "I keep waking up at three. The same three, the same dream."
  "The dream comes back. The door's always open, a little."

# ---- ALLY_ASK ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.ally_ask.more guard: beat=ally_ask act: ask_opinion
  "{you}, you saw it. Tell them what you saw."
  "Be fair, {you}. Be fair, and agree with me."
  "{you}, swing vote. The whole room's counting on you."
  "I'd love an impartial opinion, {you}. Preferably mine."
  "Settle it, {you}. A coin would be quicker, but you're nicer."

# ---- STORY --------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.story.more guard: beat=story act: tell
  "Did you see the sky last night? It turned a shade I don't like."
  "The bells rang once, and nobody was near them."
  "Folks keep leaving doors unlocked. I keep locking them."
  "Something's up with the park. The swings are too still."
  "I had an odd dream about the church. It had a staircase."
  "The fog changed direction today. It never does that."

# ---- GAME ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.game.more guard: beat=game act: ask_about
  "Quick quiz. What's the capital of snacks? Think hard."
  "Would you rather sneeze glitter or hiccup bubbles?"
  "Name three soups. Go. You have a spoon's worth of time."
  "Guess what I'm thinking. Hint: it's round and warm."
  "Rock, paper, biscuit. Winner picks the next topic."
  "Two truths and a fib, {you}. I'll start. I have the fib."

# ---- KID_MOMENT ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.kid_moment.more guard: beat=kid_moment&kid_speaker tags: kid act: tell
  "I can hold my breath for ten whole seconds! Watch."
  "I drew a cat. It looks like a potato. A fast potato."
  "Can we have a snack now? A small snack. A medium snack."
  "I'm not tired. I'm just lying down very hard."

# ---- ROMANCE_ADULT (adults the gate passed, with the one addressed saying yes) ------------------
@rule beat.romance_adult.more guard: beat=romance_adult&consent&adults_only&!kid_present&!pet act: flirt
  "I'd share my last biscuit with you, {you}. That's serious."
  "You smell like toast. I mean it as the highest praise."
  "Sit closer, {you}. The draft is my excuse."

# ---- WIND_DOWN -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule beat.wind_down.more guard: beat=wind_down act: farewell
  "That was lovely. Nobody lied much."
  "I'm out of words. I'll buy more tomorrow."
  "Time flew. I waved."
  "I think I'm done. My hat says so."
  "Thanks for this. I'll replay it at bedtime."
  "Well. The couch is calling. It's persuasive."
@rule beat.wind_down.promise.more guard: beat=wind_down act: promise
  "Visit again, {you}. I'll warm the chair."
  "Next time, I'll bring a pie. Or I'll try."
  "See you soon, {you}. Don't be a stranger. Be a regular."

# ---- idle chatter, one resident to another ------------------------------------------------------
@rule idle.ask.more guard: to_res&topic act: ask_about
  "Hey {them}. Be honest. {x:cap}: good or bad?"
  "{them}, quick. Say one thing about {x}."
  "So, {them}. What's your story with {x}?"
@rule idle.plain.more guard: to_res act: ask_about
  "{them}, did you sleep? Or did you rest?"
  "How's the knee, {them}? I'm asking for the knee."
  "{them}, got any news? Fake news is fine."
@rule idle.tease.more guard: to_res&rel=rival act: tease
  "Good silence, {them}. You've been practising."
  "{them}, nice shirt. Is it the same one?"
@rule idle.muse.more guard: !to_res act: tell
  "I'm just going to look at the ceiling. It's got character."
  "The floor is doing its thing again."
  "Does anyone hear that? Neither do I. Peaceful."

# ---- the prod ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule prod.more act: ask_feeling
  "Cat got your tongue, {you}? Hand it back when you can."
  "Hello? The room is waiting, {you}. Gently."
  "{you}, we're all looking at you. In a kind way."
  "Any thoughts, {you}? Even half a thought."

# ---- walking out -----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule excuse.more act: farewell
  "I need to go feed something. Not sure what."
  "My nap is booked. I'd hate to miss it."
  "Gotta run. The kettle's calling."
  "I've got a meeting with my couch. Bye."
  "Sorry, I just remembered an appointment. With a sandwich."

# ---- cut off by another resident ----------------------------------------------------------------
@rule grumble.more act: complain
  "Hey, I wasn't finished. I was warming up."
  "Hmph. I'll just write it down for later."
  "That was my turn. I had a good ending."
  "Fine. Interrupt away. I'll be over here, sulking."

# ---- an argument: the jab -----------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule jab.more guard: to_res act: tease
  "Oh, {them}, you're so wise. Your hat is, at least."
  "Bold words, {them}. Bold hat, too."
  "That's nice, {them}. Did you think of that yourself?"
  "Interesting take, {them}. Did it come with a warranty?"

# ---- step 2: the row -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule row.more guard: to_res&!kid_present act: accuse
  "You never listen, {them}. You never, ever listen."
  "I've had it with you, {them}. Up to here. Higher."
  "Don't {them} me. You know what you did."

# ---- step 3: the ultimatum -----------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule ultimatum.more guard: to_res&!kid_present act: ask_opinion
  "{you}, whose side? Mine or {them}'s? Quick."
  "I'm done, {you}. Tell {them} they're wrong. Please."
  "Pick one, {you}. I'll wait. I'll wait loudly."

# ---- making up ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
@rule makeup.more guard: to_res act: apologize
  "Sorry, {them}. I was grumpy. Mostly at the weather."
  "Okay, {them}. You win. A little, don't gloat."
  "I take it back, {them}. Most of it. Some."

# ---- a child in the room of an argument -------------------------------------------------------
@rule kidask.more guard: kid_speaker tags: kid act: ask_feeling
  "Why's everyone shouty? Did someone take a biscuit?"
  "Can you two be nice? I want you both."
  "Is this a game? It's not a fun game."
